-         Two overloads which share the name: the companion's constructor over a fresh
-         `AtomicReference`, and the extension `cell()`, a volatile read which needs no `nn` and
-         does not throw on a cell holding `Unset`.
-     entry .vacant   `Atomic.Ref.vacant[value]`: an initially-absent `Ref[Optional[value]]`
-     entry .update   `cell() = value`: a volatile store to an `Atomic.Ref`
-     entry .publish   `cell.publish(value)`: a release store (`lazySet`) to an `Atomic.Ref`
-     entry .swap   `cell.swap(value)`: stores a value in an `Atomic.Ref` and returns the one displaced
-     entry .replace   `cell.replace(expected, updated)`: compare-and-set by reference equality, true if it took
-     entry .ere   applies a transition to an `Atomic.Ref` (or stores a value) and returns the value displaced
-     entry .since   applies a transition to an `Atomic.Ref` and returns the value installed
-     entry .revise   applies a transition which is a function value, not a literal, and returns the value installed
-         The escape hatch for a transition whose shape cannot be inspected — a function passed as
-         a parameter. It runs a compare-and-set loop, so the transition may be re-run under
-         contention and must be pure; a transition which returns the same reference settles
-         without writing.
